{"kind":"stack","id":"s-circuits","title":"Will the lamp light? Complete loops and simple circuits","theme":{"background":"#fdfbf4","foreground":"#1d2a3a","font":"Trebuchet MS, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Circuit"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"A closed loop that a current can travel around, from a battery through parts and back to the battery."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"bulb"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"A lamp is connected to one battery with a wire at each end. Is the loop complete?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"No, there is a gap in the loop","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Yes, the loop is complete","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"Only if the lamp is switched off","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Where does the current start in a simple circuit?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"At the lamp","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"At the battery","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"At the wire end","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"A wire has a break in it. Will the lamp light?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Yes, the lamp still lights","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"No, the loop is no longer complete","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"It lights, but only a little","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Mia builds a circuit. Her lamp is dark. Which way should she go?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Check the loop for a gap","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Add a second lamp","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Mia finds a loose wire and reconnects it. The lamp lights up. Well done, Mia!"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Mia adds a second lamp, but the loop still has a gap. Neither lamp lights."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Which of these is a complete loop with a battery?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"A lamp with one wire, not joined to the battery","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"A battery, a lamp and wires joined end to end","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"A battery with a wire lying loose beside it","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"Open circuit"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-e","content":"A circuit with a gap in it, so the current cannot flow and the lamp stays off."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which word describes a circuit with a gap in it?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Closed","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Open","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Charged","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-q","content":"Pupils test three circuits. Which one will light the lamp?"},{"type":"button","id":"c11-a","label":"Battery and lamp joined by one wire only","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-b","label":"Battery, lamp and two wires forming a full loop","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-c","label":"Lamp alone with no battery","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c12","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c12-h","content":"Well done! You have finished the circuits quiz."},{"type":"text","id":"c12-m","content":"You now know a lamp lights only when it is part of a complete loop with a battery."}],"actions":[]}}
